WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.350
- For as long as there's been crime,

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.500
there have been criminals
bragging about those crimes.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.840
Smartphones record our daily lives,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.070
and some of our daily lives

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.016
include a whole bunch of criming.

00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:11.160
(TV static)
(beep)

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.390
Hey, what's up guys?

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.830
Welcome back to Illegal Eagle.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.450
Today I stole 50k Bitcoin

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.970
and used it to hire a
hitman because it's fun.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.280
This is why you should take
legal advice from a YouTuber.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.510
Remember to like and subscribe

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.475
and always brag about your
crimes online and to the police.

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:25.380
(beep)

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.460
And I can't remember who said it,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.720
but it's a strange coincidence

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.820
that as soon as we all had video cameras

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.890
in our own pockets 24/7,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.880
ghosts disappeared,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.200
aliens stopped visiting,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.660
and police started
shooting unarmed people.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.070
But while the phones may be smart,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.750
the criminals are still really dumb,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.790
so today we're gonna cover some
of those stunning instances

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.280
where criminals might just
have gotten away with it

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.590
if it weren't for those
meddling smartphones.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.080
Now, selfies are not just
about making dumb faces

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.510
with a dream of gaining
Instagram influence.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.360
Selfies also have helped bring
dumb criminals to justice.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.070
Like 19 year old Albert Wilson,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.750
who stole a phone, took a selfie,

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.120
and then tattled on himself
by accidentally emailing

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.040
his own photo to the victim.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.360
And here's how it all went down.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.250
One fateful Saturday night in 2013,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.960
Albert Wilson and five accomplices

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.700
surrounded a 16 year old boy in the Bronx,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.920
ordering the victim to empty his pockets.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.270
Wilson proceeded to grab

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.680
the teen's Samsung
Galaxy S Epic smartphone

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
before fleeing with his fellow thieves.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.230
But the mystery of who
stole the teen's phone

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.200
would not last very long because
shortly after the robbery,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.660
Wilson could not help but
test the photographic quality

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.180
of the Samsung Galaxy
by snapping his selfie.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.070
But honestly, that's not surprising.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.430
Hey, Rene, how good was the
Samsung Galaxy S's camera?

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.910
- Well, Devin, Samsung is
actually the perfect camera

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.530
for recording your crimes.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.980
Unlike Google, which focuses
its massive AI powers

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.020
on computational photography,

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.750
or Apple, which tries to
do a little bit of both,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.730
Samsung has just always been
all in on sheer optical girth,

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.420
just massive and multiple
lenses grafted front and back

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.610
with conveniently pre-crushed blacks.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.410
- That's a color correction term.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.368
- And auto boosted sat for all your

00:02:00.368 --> 00:02:02.280
ready-to-social criming needs.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.113
- There you have criminals.

00:02:03.113 --> 00:02:04.470
If you're going to crime,

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.060
you definitely use a Samsung.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.680
But what Wilson did not know,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.140
the phone was set to automatically
upload all photographs

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.970
to the teen victim's email account.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.970
And with a literal photo
ID of the teen attacker

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.320
in his inbox,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.110
well, the victim immediately
took that selfie to the police.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.520
Wilson was swiftly arrested

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.070
and charged with robbery,
possession of stolen property,

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.939
and a controlled substance
believed to be crack cocaine.

00:02:25.939 --> 00:02:27.600
- Oh, I'm sorry!
- Oh! Oh!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.040
- Did you get addicted to crack?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.480
Did somebody get addicted to crack?

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.070
- So thanks to Wilson's selfie,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.060
justice was served.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.480
Now, I know that this is
the least important part

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.470
of the story,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.050
but I have to remark that Wilson

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.820
has an absolutely terrible selfie game.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.920
I mean, just look at this travesty.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.030
I mean, the photo is hazy,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.100
you can see the phone's
reflection in the glasses,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.676
and you know, why are
you wearing headphones?

00:02:49.676 --> 00:02:50.907
♪ I fought the law ♪

00:02:50.907 --> 00:02:52.659
♪ And the law won ♪

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:54.420
So honestly, six outta 10,

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.340
though bonus points for taking a photo

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.830
in front of a sign that says "Arrest".

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.600
Anyway, our next criminal
might be even dumber

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.060
because he posts a photo
of himself siphoning gas

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.410
out of a cop car.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.380
Now, when it comes to
dealing with high gas prices,

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.720
there are many ways to
lessen the pain of the pump.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.340
Some opt to take public transit,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.080
others have elected to switch to electric

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.760
or hybrid vehicles.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.010
But one Kentucky man decided to engage

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.320
in his own amateur oil exploration

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.890
by siphoning gas directly
from a police officer's car

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.190
and then brag about his crime on Facebook.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.490
And I'm sure that you can guess
exactly how that turned out.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.830
So in 2012, a 20 year
old Kentucky resident

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.940
Michael Baker and his girlfriend

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.700
stumbled upon an unattended
Jenkins Police vehicle,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.460
and seizing the opportunity
for some free fuel,

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.460
Baker proceeded to siphon
gas from the squad car.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.290
And he might have gotten away with it,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.870
except Baker couldn't resist the urge

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.730
to have his girlfriend snap a photo

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.710
that showed him, not only stealing gas,

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.120
but also flipping the bird.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.320
And then he memorialized it
by posting it to Facebook.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.007
Now, there's the old proverb that goes,

00:03:57.007 --> 00:03:59.100
"Pride cometh before the fall",

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.800
and also, "Only idiots post to Facebook."

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.550
But this cocky Kentuckian was
done in by his own vanity.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.590
After bragging about
his crimes on Facebook,

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.960
the county issued a
warrant for Baker's arrest.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:10.793
One month later,

00:04:10.793 --> 00:04:11.970
Baker was taken into custody

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.680
and charged with misdemeanor and theft.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.970
- Well, we was just standing there

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:18.090
and I thought it'd be funny take picture

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.520
and then we post it on Facebook.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.500
- Yeah, we're sorry.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.620
It was just a joke.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.880
I mean, if we was gonna steal gas,

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.980
we wouldn't put it nationwide on Facebook.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.530
I mean, we don't steal anyway, but.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.480
- And although the
siphoning photo was removed

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.710
from his Facebook page,

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.410
Baker managed to keep
his 380 friends apprised

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.610
of his latest legal problems,

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.290
quote, "just got out of jail."

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.460
he wrote in one post.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.177
And another post he wrote, quote,

00:04:40.177 --> 00:04:44.040
"Yeah, lol, I went to jail over Facebook."

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:44.970
And in response to a friend

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.680
who had not seen the image
before it was removed,

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.737
Baker assured, quote,

00:04:47.737 --> 00:04:51.030
"Yeah, lol, you just have to seen it.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.770
It was funny as hell though."

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.251
- [Reporter] So I mean, do you
apologize to the cops for it?

00:04:56.251 --> 00:04:57.866
("The Next Episode" by Dr. Dre plays)

00:04:57.866 --> 00:04:58.827
- Not really.

00:04:58.827 --> 00:05:00.300
- And then moving one state over,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.250
we had the Tennessee man
who attached an Apple watch

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.280
to his girlfriend's car in
order to try to stalk her.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.557
Now Apple markets the
Apple watch as, quote,

00:05:08.557 --> 00:05:10.770
"The ultimate choice for a healthy life."

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.240
Now, the Apple Watch boast a variety

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.800
of health and safety
features for its users.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.690
The Apple Watch can track your heart rate,

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.650
track your workouts,

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.210
can even be used with air tags track items

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.170
you might have misplaced,

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.440
items like your girlfriend.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.710
Yeah, unfortunately, a
Nashville man decided

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.060
to use the Apple Watch
for nefarious purposes,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.500
to track his girlfriends every move

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.080
and stalk her with watch's
location technology.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.030
Now, thankfully, police
were able to intervene

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.320
before anything dire happened.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.960
According to the March, 2022 affidavit,

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.360
Welch's girlfriend visited
the Family Service Center,

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.490
a domestic violence shelter,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.500
to seek a restraining order against him.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.910
Now, police officers were summoned

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.140
to the Family Safety Center

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:48.300
after security informed
them of Welch's presence.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.370
But remember, tracking goes both ways.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.590
When the police inspected
the victim's car,

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.810
they found an Apple Watch
attached to the spokes

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.400
of the car's wheel,

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.980
and they were able to
link that to the person

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.870
who was trying to track her.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:01.703
But funny story,

00:06:01.703 --> 00:06:02.640
this is actually very similar

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.130
to how I keep track of
Rene Ritchie at all times.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.890
- [Rene] I've been using an
Apple Watch all day, every day.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.480
- But then there's the Ohio man who sent

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.220
in a selfie of himself to police

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.700
to replace the terrible
mugshot that they took of him.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.960
These frigging people.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.570
Anyway, you know when most
people get a bad picture,

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.010
whether it's on a driver's license

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.097
or for a school photo,

00:06:21.097 --> 00:06:22.830
you know, they just take the loss

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.870
and hope for a better
picture the next time around.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.630
But Ohio man, Donald Chip Pugh,

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:28.650
learned the hard way

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.390
that when you're on the run from the law,

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.550
maybe that's not the best
time to contact the police

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.140
to complain about your mugshot.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.060
- Pablo didn't know it then,

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.880
but this mugshot was gonna
cause him a lot of grief

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:39.810
down the line.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.310
- Unless your goal is to assist the police

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.360
with your capture,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.130
which, of course, is exactly what happened

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.870
in this particular case.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.390
In 2016, Pugh was scheduled
to appear in court

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.700
for a pending DUI charge in Lima, Ohio.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.320
And when Pugh skipped his hearing,

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.560
local police posted
the mugshot on Facebook

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.970
to solicit the public's
help in tracking him down.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.640
Quote, "Mr. Pugh is also
currently a person of interest

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.200
in several other cases,"

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.480
including for arson and vandalism.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.820
Now, Pugh saw his mugshot and was furious,

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.890
not that the police were
trying to track him down

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.500
or that he committed multiple crimes,

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.370
but that his picture had failed
to capture his good side.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.540
So Pugh took the initiative.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.000
Dressed himself up in a
houndstooth pattern suit,

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.400
not unlike the one that
I'm wearing right now,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.297
put on some sunglasses
and texted the police,

00:07:22.297 --> 00:07:25.170
"Here's a better photo
that one is terrible"

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.760
with an accompanying selfie.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.220
Now, Pugh was no stranger to
the Lima Police Department,

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.480
having had previous run-ins

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.340
that included charges
of disorderly conduct,

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.210
breaking and entering,

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.560
and domestic violence.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.630
But this was the first time
that Pugh had ever reached out

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.330
to the police while they
had an active arrest warrant

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.953
for his arrest.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:45.030
Now, the Lima Police
honored Pugh's request,

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.527
uploading his new mugshot to
Facebook and writing, quote,

00:07:47.527 --> 00:07:49.320
"We thank him for being helpful,

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.580
but now we would appreciate it

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.510
if he would come speak to us
at the LPD about his charges."

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.460
Now, a smart criminal might lay low

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.290
to avoid drawing attention to themselves,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.050
but this video is not
about smart criminals.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:01.883
And as it turns out,

00:08:01.883 --> 00:08:04.320
Pugh was not done talking
about what he considered

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.050
to be a grave injustice
of an unflattering photo.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.820
So after Pugh's mugshot and selfie

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.410
began circulating on the internet,

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:13.290
he decided to call into
Lima's classic rock station

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.600
1040.9 The Eagle,
(eagle screech)

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.040
to tell his side of the story.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.600
Now, the local station spoke to Pugh

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.490
for its "Idiot Of The Day" segment,

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:22.380
and as it turns out, Pugh had the honor

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.990
of being the first idiot to
ever be interviewed on air.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.000
- Where you at again, Chip?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.260
- Right now?

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:29.093
- Yeah.

00:08:29.093 --> 00:08:29.970
- Actually I'm sitting in a bunker

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.470
right next to Chapo Guzman.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.050
We're trying to dig a tunnel
and get to McDonald's.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.860
- But sadly, Pugh's run from
the law did not last very long.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.110
The next morning, Pugh was
arrested 800 miles away

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.430
in Century Florida,

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:44.010
because at heart we all
knew that this Ohio man

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.630
was really a Florida man.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.950
- In Ohio,

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:47.910
Northern Florida.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:48.840
I mean, let's be honest,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.767
they're really like angling for that

00:08:50.767 --> 00:08:52.500
"weird stuff happens here".

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.430
- But ladies and gentlemen,

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:55.980
there is a happy ending to this story.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.870
When Pugh was arrested in Florida,

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.390
he got to take his mugshot over again.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.410
Though I have to admit,

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.270
I don't think that that's
much of an improvement

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.350
over his first one.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.450
Now sometimes criminals
are incredibly stupid,

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.540
but sometimes the police are
just really, really smart.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:10.860
And such was the case when the FBI

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.480
actually created a fake messaging app

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.010
and then got a whole bunch of criminals

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.770
to use the fake encrypted messaging app.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.450
Because most of the cases
we've talked about today

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.090
involve criminals using
smartphones to tell on themselves.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.010
But when it comes to
the more savvy criminals

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:26.100
who are actually trying not to
get caught committing crimes,

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.230
these folks often turn
to encrypted messaging

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.430
to cover their tracks

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:30.540
and shield their communications

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.670
from the prying eyes of law enforcement.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.230
That's because when
messages are encrypted,

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.300
it's nearly impossible for law enforcement

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.280
to learn what criminal groups are doing.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.230
So when faced with encrypted messaging,

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:41.940
what is law enforcement to do?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.320
Well, simple.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.630
Develop their own fake
encrypted messaging app,

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:48.450
trick criminal organizations
into downloading the fake app,

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.960
and wait for the incriminating
evidence to just roll in.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.160
And that was the work of what was known as

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.540
Operation Trojan Shield,

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.330
a successful multi-year
electronic sting operation

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.300
led by the FBI in
conjunction with the DEA,

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.790
EUROPOL, the European Police Agency,

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.730
and law enforcement groups
from 16 other countries,

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.970
because in 2018, the FBI and
its international partners

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.590
shut down Phantom Secure,

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.380
a Canadian based company that
provided secure communications

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.790
to high level drug traffickers

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.680
in other criminal organizations.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.150
The company would purchase smartphones,

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.640
wipe them clean of all traditional
functions like texting,

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:21.960
internet, and GPS,

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.300
and then it installed
encrypted email systems

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.220
that could only communicate with other

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.690
Phantom Secure phones.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.490
And if a customer was arrested,

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:32.700
Phantom Secure would destroy
all data on the phone.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.130
Now, after the feds shut
down Phantom Secure,

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:38.550
the CEO, Vincent Ramos, was
then indicted by a grand jury

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:39.600
along with his colleagues,

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.120
and would eventually plead
guilty to a raft of charges

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.680
related to drug trafficking.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:44.880
And with Phantom Secure gone,

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:48.060
criminals were in search of a
new encrypted messaging app,

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.940
and that's where Operation
Trojan Shield comes in.

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.350
Now, at the beginning of the operation,

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:54.360
the FBI recruited an unnamed confidential

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.150
human source who had been
developing a next generation

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.460
secure messaging platform
for the criminal underworld

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.360
called ANOM.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.220
Now, the app would only
work on specially modified

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.800
cell phones similar to those
created by Phantom Secure.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.180
But what the users didn't know,

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.100
the mystery developer had engineered ANOM

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.260
to secretly forward law enforcement a copy

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.810
of every message that
was sent on the platform.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.360
After an ANOM's launch in October 2019,

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.010
the FBI convinced a few criminals

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.510
to tell others about the phones,

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:21.510
and soon enough the app
caught on like wildfire.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.650
In an 18 month period,

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:25.830
law enforcement provided
nearly 12,000 ANOM phones

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.120
through unsuspecting middlemen

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.670
to more than 300 criminal syndicates

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.410
in more than 100 countries.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.180
And many of the criminals
assured each other

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.430
that the app was incredibly safe.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.570
But rather than being safe,

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.210
police in real time could
read criminals discussing

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.910
targeted hits, drug
shipments, and other crimes,

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:44.550
with users making no attempt
to hide criminal plots

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.480
with code words.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.540
And between October 2019 and June 2021,

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:52.560
authorities collected more
than 27 million messages

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.940
in 45 languages.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.390
And armed with this treasure
trove of incriminating data,

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.670
the FBI and its 16 international partners

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.980
carried out raids in their
respective countries.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.150
In a 48 hour period,

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.820
9,000 officers deployed
worldwide to make arrests

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.160
and search more than 700 locations.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.090
According to the FBI,

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:11.700
more than 32 tons of drugs were seized,

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:12.600
killjoys,

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.650
along with 250 firearms
and 48 million in cash.

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.930
And more than 50 secret
drug labs were dismantled,

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.060
including one of the
largest clandestine labs

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.500
in German history.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:26.220
In total, Operation Trojan
Shield resulted in 800 arrests,

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.160
including 500 in the 48 hour period.

